==Finnish==

===Etymology===
A twentieth century invention usually interpreted as a variant of {{m|fi|Saara||Sarah}}, rhyming with other popular 1960s names, {{m|fi|Ari}}, {{m|fi|Jari}} and {{m|fi|Mari}}. Other possible sources are the place name {{m|fi|Sariola}} in the [[Kalevala]], and Hungarian {{m|hu|Sári}} (a pet form of {{m|hu|Sára}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈsɑri]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|Sa|ri|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑri|lang=fi}}.

